# Working handover for whoever picks this up, including a future me after a
# compaction. Machine-local paths and in-flight state; it describes the working
# session, not the repository.
docs/HANDOVER.md

# Machine-local cargo overrides.
#
# `.cargo/config.toml` is tracked and has to stay tracked: it carries the macOS
# link flags and the usvg patch that every build needs. What must never be
# committed is the `[patch]` block that redirects the renderer packages to
# working checkouts, because the paths in it exist on one machine.
#
# This line alone does nothing, since git does not consult .gitignore for a
# tracked path. It is the pair to the command in AGENTS.md:
#
#     git update-index --skip-worktree .cargo/config.toml
#
# That is what makes local edits invisible to `git status` and `git add -A`. The
# entry here covers the other direction, if the file is ever untracked.
.cargo/config.toml

# Renderer redirect for local builds. Untracked on purpose: the paths exist on
# one machine. See scripts/local-renderer.sh.
.cargo/local-renderer.toml

# Handover docs are working notes, never committed. See AGENTS.md.
docs/HANDOVER.md
HANDOVER*.md
# Operator runbooks: machine-local paths and one-off recovery state.
docs/restore.md
docs/RESTORE*.md
